12.3	Absorption
The absolute bioavailability of acamprosate calcium after oral administration is about 11%. Steady-state plasma concentrations of acamprosate are reached within 5 days of dosing. Steady-state peak plasma concentrations after acamprosate calcium doses of 2 x 333 mg tablets three times daily average 350 ng/mL and occur at 3 to 8 hours post-dose. Coadministration of acamprosate calcium with food decreases bioavailability as measured by Cmax and AUC, by approximately 42% and 23%, respectively. The food effect on absorption is not clinically significant and no adjustment of dose is necessary.
