[?2004h>         "status": "ANSWERED",
[?2004le_or_s[?2004h>         "answer": "Comparing ACETAMINOPHEN with CODEINE and AcetaZOLAMIDE: ACETAMINOPHEN with CODEINE tablets are administered orally at a dose of 1 to 2 tablets every 6-8 hours as needed (repeated up to every 4 hours) for pain in adults, with a maximum daily dose determined by the prescriber based on the guidance (not to exceed 4000 mg of acetaminophen). AcetaZOLAMIDE is administered orally at doses ranging from 250 mg to 1000 mg daily (either once daily or in divided doses depending on the indication such as glaucoma, epilepsy, congestive heart failure, or acute mountain sickness) for adults and children, with a maximum daily dose of 1000 mg (1 g) stated as the limit above which no increased effect is produced for glaucoma and epilepsy.",
