[?2004l[?2004h>         "answer": "Comparing Acyclovir and Acyclovir suspension: Both formulations contain acyclovir and share the same dosing instructions. For acute treatment of herpes zoster, the dose is 800 mg orally every 4 hours, 5 times daily for 7 to 10 days. For initial genital herpes, the dose is 200 mg every 4 hours, 5 times daily for 10 days. Chronic suppressive therapy is 400 mg twice daily. Chickenpox dosing for children (2 years and older) is 20 mg/kg per dose 4 times daily, and for adults and children over 40 kg is 800 mg 4 times daily for 5 days. The maximum daily dose is 4000 mg (800 mg 5 times daily) for herpes zoster, 1000 mg (200 mg 5 times daily) for genital herpes, and 3200 mg for chickenpox.",
